# netsurf: built-ins are shaped as built-ins -- no prototype on operations
# and accessors, accessors named "get x", interface tags, no fileName
# (patch 275)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 274)
#
# A browser's operations and attribute accessors are built-in functions:
# no prototype property, not constructors, an accessor named for its
# attribute ("get userAgent"). Here 504 of 870 operations on window and the
# interface prototypes carried a prototype property (they are written in
# JavaScript), 542 of 575 accessors were anonymous or named "get", and
# Object.getOwnPropertyNames(toDataURL) gave length, name, prototype --
# Chromium length, name; hsw reads exactly that.
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: each such function becomes a
#    method-shaped stand-in (a method has no prototype and is no
#    constructor) calling the original, with its name and length; a native
#    one only gets its name, and one serving several attributes
#    (textContent / nodeValue / data) keeps it for the first and a stand-in
#    for the others. On window, every interface prototype and static, the
#    bridge's own layers in a node's prototype chain (its wrapper class,
#    per-node prototypes) and navigator, document, screen, performance,
#    history, location, crypto, console, CSS, the storages. Internal
#    members (_x, __x) are left as they are. A stand-in carries the marks
#    this file puts on its wrappers (__vbCD, __vbNat, ...), so a later pass
#    still sees one is wrapped (without that the characterData setter was
#    wrapped twice and JS-chardata saw 4 records for 2 writes).
#  - every interface prototype carries its own @@toStringTag (patch 269
#    tagged only those that printed [object Object], so a DOM interface
#    inherited EventTarget's: String(document.body) was
#    "[object EventTarget]", now "[object HTMLBodyElement]").
#  - 18 accessors this file defined without configurable (Response,
#    Request, TextEncoder / TextDecoder, the streams, IDBDatabase) are
#    configurable and enumerable, as WebIDL attributes are; that is also
#    what lets them be reshaped.
#  - QuickJS's Function.prototype.fileName / lineNumber / columnNumber are
#    deleted (no browser has them; nothing here used them).
#
# Found by the hCaptcha record/compare (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md,
# "Record, replay"); not the refusal (the demo still refuses).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-builtin-shape.html (BSHAPE 8/8, Chromium 8/8;
# the build before fails 1, 3, 4, 5, 8).
